description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts, stop re-dispatching gaps whose quoted anchor no longer exists in the file they name.

The file contains exactly one occurrence of this line, inside admitActionableGaps:
    const failedAttempts = Number(meta.failed_attempts ?? 0);

Insert the following block immediately after that line, keeping the existing line unchanged:

    // (E3) PHANTOM ANCHOR — retire a gap whose quoted anchor is already gone from the file
    // it names. Measured 2026-09-11: 17 of 600 open gaps cite a complete anchor with zero
    // occurrences in their named file, so every retry must fail anchor_not_found forever.
    // FAIL-OPEN by construction: any parse, path or read problem admits exactly as before.
    try {
      const phantomSummary = String(g.summary ?? "");
      const phantomAnchor = phantomSummary
        .split(String.fromCharCode(10))
        .map((l) => l.trim())
        .find((l) => (l.startsWith("const ") || l.startsWith("let ") || l.startsWith("function ")) && l.endsWith(";") && l.length > 20);
      const phantomSite = String(meta.edit_site ?? "").split(":")[0];
      if (phantomAnchor && phantomSite.startsWith("repos/") && failedAttempts >= 2) {
        const phantomRoot = process.env["VESSELS_CLONE_ROOT"] ?? "/workspace/git/vessels";
        const phantomParts = phantomSite.split("/");
        const phantomAbs = phantomRoot + "/" + phantomParts[1] + "/" + phantomParts.slice(2).join("/");
        if (existsSync(phantomAbs) && !readFileSync(phantomAbs, "utf8").includes(phantomAnchor)) {
          excluded.push({ id, reason: "phantom_anchor(" + phantomParts[1] + ")" });
          continue;
        }
      }
    } catch { /* fail-open: admit as before */ }

One file, one insertion. Do not modify the existing line, any other line, or any other file. The inserted block contains no backslash characters; copy it exactly.

WHY. A gap that quotes an anchor which is no longer present in its target file can never succeed: every attempt fails anchor_not_found, the gap is retried, and a chronically-stuck escalation mints narrowed children that inherit the same impossible instruction. Measured on the live gap store 2026-09-11 by extracting 137 complete quoted anchors from open gaps and grepping each against its named file: 17 of 600 open gaps, 2.8 percent, cite an anchor with ZERO occurrences. One of them, route-edit-2463d13c, quotes if (process.env.EXEMPLAR_SELECTOR_RUN_ON_BOOT === 'true') { which was replaced earlier that day by commit 7c34185, so the gap was re-attempting completed work.

These failures are indistinguishable from drafter defects in the traces, which is why they persisted: the compose reports anchor_not_found and the gap looks like a hard authoring problem rather than a stale instruction.

SAFETY. The block is additive and fail-open. It is wrapped in try/catch and every guard admits on doubt: it acts only when the summary contains a complete declaration line longer than 20 characters ending in a semicolon, the edit_site names a repos/ path, the gap has already failed at least twice, the resolved file exists, and the anchor is genuinely absent. Any other condition, including a missing file, an unparseable edit_site or a read error, leaves the gap admitted exactly as today. It uses only existsSync and readFileSync, which are already imported at the top of this file. It deliberately does not call vesselsCloneRoot because that helper is declared later in the file and calling it here would be a use-before-declaration error.

Verified by execution against a temporary tree covering six cases: an absent anchor with two failed attempts is excluded; a present anchor is admitted; a gap with zero failed attempts is admitted; a missing file is admitted; a summary with no anchor is admitted; and a null edit_site is admitted.

